.0037,"etf":"XLP"}}],"quotes":[{"c":"USFD 2019 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2019-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"And generally speaking, able to pass it through, you can't have some time delays depending on the significance at any point in time, but nothing beyond, which we normally expect.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2019-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Heinbockel","x":"Is that -- when you think about the timing of pass-through, was that just the way to step up on some of those items?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2019-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"And as Pietro noted, we are reiterating our outlook for the full year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2019-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"For fiscal-year 2019, we are reiterating our outlook as I mentioned earlier, that we provided in February.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2019-08-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"Our business performance in the second quarter continued the positive momentum we experienced in the first quarter, and we are reiterating our guidance for the full year as Pietro noted.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/06/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2019-08-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"For fiscal 2019, we are reiterating the guidance ranges that we provided in February but do expect to be toward the high end of adjusted diluted EPS range and at the low end of the interest expense range.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/06/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2020-02-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"So overall, not a big change, and we didn't see anything different in the quarter that really impacted our ability to pass it through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2019 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2020-02-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"This is with our customers, and so that predominantly relates to pass-through of product cost.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2020-05-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"…is really managing through that, trying to do it effectively as when we talk a lot of times in the center of the flight, it's really a benefit of most of our businesses that tends to be passed through, and it's just a matter of contract being a set duration or through reps passing that through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/06/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2020-05-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"In distribution which accounts for the majority of our operating expenses, we quickly accomplished the rightsizing of our cost structure through a combination of furloughs, and temporarily contracting some of our drivers and selectors to retailers who have experienced a surge in demand.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/06/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2020-05-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"And that's because again as we expect a lower, smaller number of customers due to some closures, we wanted to rightsize the sales force and ensure we put our best talent forward as the sector recovers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/06/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"What I would say is, to date, though, we have used some combination of permanent and temporary reductions and continue to use both of these as we ensure our cost structure right size for our business and just we'll continue to evaluate.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/04/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Karru Martinson","x":"And then just lastly, you saw a larger regional filed Chapter 11 and going into restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/04/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q3","e":"usfd","d":"2020-11-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"And finally, the steady improvement in our case volume, combined with our cost reduction actions, led to adjusted EBITDA that was a marked improvement over the second quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/02/us-foods-holding-usfd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q3","e":"usfd","d":"2020-11-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"I think the other incremental piece is we would expect a little more of the cost savings to show up in Q4.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/02/us-foods-holding-usfd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2021-02-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"And then, what you find is in the noncontract business, it -- we tend to be able to pass it through relatively quickly.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2021-02-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"The things that can make it a little bit longer is if you have one particular class that significantly inflates and maybe it takes, instead of a couple of weeks, it takes three or four weeks, but generally able to pass it through and not have an impact overall on our gross margins.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2021-02-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"This does not change the cost savings that we announced in August but is simply a logical evolution of our operating model, informed by the experiences of the last 12 months, and they end up providing more consistent execution.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2020 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2021-02-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"I think it's too early to tell, but I think the way you're thinking about it is definitely the right way to think about it, is we would expect it to be sooner because of the cost reduction opportunity that we took advantage of last year and the improvements that that drives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2021-05-10","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"Same-store sales for April are ahead of 2019 as restaurant demand continues to recover and we continue to benefit from some direct-to-consumer sales, sales that we are getting without modifying our business model.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/10/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2021-05-10","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"And so, on the local side, so with the inflation, to your point, the combination, normally, in an inflationary environments, you can see some compression when net inflation happens for the -- immediately, and then it gets passed through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/10/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2021-05-10","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"…teams have worked very, very closely and have done a really nice job through here of really taking, sort of managing that very well to be able to pass through that inflation and gain a little bit of pricing as we've gone through there, but again, trying to price very fairly to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/10/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2021-05-10","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"On opex, over the last few quarters, I've spoken about the $180 million of fixed cost savings that we enacted in 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/10/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2021-05-10","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"These cost savings are contributing to our results, and we are beginning to see the fixed cost leverage return as case volume recovers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/10/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2021-08-09","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"Our team has done an excellent job of managing that inflation and passing it through to customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/09/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2021-08-09","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"And as you see our ability to pass that through with really the gross profit per case being above 2019.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/09/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q3","e":"usfd","d":"2021-11-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"Contributing to this expansion, gross profit has been, first, our ability to manage and pass through inflation; second, continued growth in private label brands; and third, the continued optimization of terms and customers in our portfolio.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/08/us-foods-holding-usfd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q3","e":"usfd","d":"2021-11-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"Our team continued to do an excellent job of managing that inflation and effectively passing it through to customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/08/us-foods-holding-usfd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q3","e":"usfd","d":"2021-11-08","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"Lastly, on the sales and administrative side, we still expect to retain two-thirds of the $180 million in fixed cost savings that we announced last year, with most of the reinvestment showing up as an expansion in our sales force, which will drive market share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/08/us-foods-holding-usfd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q3","e":"usfd","d":"2021-11-08","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"We also have our sights firmly on returning to 2019 pro forma adjusted EBITDA and then growing from there based on M&A synergies, top-line growth, including the $1 billion of net new customer wins Pietro referenced, GP expansion and cost savings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/08/us-foods-holding-usfd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2022-02-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jake Bartlett","x":"It seems like that's been driven in part by just supply chain disruption and is driving really strong pricing power for you and your peers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/02/17/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2022-02-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"Our new operating model gives us line of sight through initiatives already underway to improve execution on cost reduction.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/02/17/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2021 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2022-02-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pietro Satriano","x":"And it also helps streamline operations, which helps contribute to improved distribution cost per case.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/02/17/us-foods-holding-usfd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2022 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2022-05-12","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"Inflation is fairly broad-based across most categories, and we have been successful in passing it through to customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/05/12/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2022-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2022 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2022-05-12","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Edward Kelly","x":"Both your peers raised guidance this quarter, Dirk, albeit they have one quarter to go.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/05/12/us-foods-holding-usfd-q1-2022-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2022 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2022-08-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"Inflation in Q2 has been more in the grocery categories and other categories, and we've continued to be successful in passing it through to customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/08/11/us-foods-holding-usfd-q2-2022-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"USFD 2025 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2026-02-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"David Flitman","x":"Furthermore, we achieved approximately $45 million in indirect cost savings in 2025.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/us-foods-usfd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2025 Q4","e":"usfd","d":"2026-02-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Peter Saleh","x":"And then just -- I think you highlighted a couple of incremental cost savings that you guys have found on cost of goods and indirect costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/us-foods-usfd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk J. Locascio","x":"It provides a small positive to distributors and is manageable for operators to pass through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/us-foods-usfd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk J. Locascio","x":"In the current environment, we have effectively passed through costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/us-foods-usfd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David E. Flitman","x":"He can cost out new menu items and try ingredient swaps in a few minutes on his phone—something that used to take hours juggling spreadsheets.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/us-foods-usfd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David E. Flitman","x":"…industry-leading products, smart technology, and support, designed to help our hospitality customers solve some of their biggest challenges: managing labor and staffing, identifying cost savings opportunities, and improving menu profitability for high-volume events such as catering and banquets.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/us-foods-usfd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q1","e":"usfd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Dirk J. Locascio","x":"Now turning to guidance on Slide 12, we are reaffirming our 2026 guidance based on the strength of our business and outlook for the balance of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/us-foods-usfd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2026-08-06","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"David Flitman","x":"Across the business -- our teams are applying a continuous improvement mindset while leveraging investments in technology, including artificial intelligence to raise customer service levels, improve productivity and create a stronger foundation for sustainable long-term growth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/us-foods-usfd-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2026-08-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dirk Locascio","x":"So say it continues to be right in that spot that we feel good about managing and passing through and that customers can handle and not all that volatile.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/us-foods-usfd-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"USFD 2026 Q2","e":"usfd","d":"2026-08-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Rahul Krotthapall